{
 "version": "20261030-175852",
 "notes": "The 2D Doodle Studio's layout comes to 3D: Canvas, Tools and Timeline docks you can swap, resize, detach to another screen or hide (Ctrl+Shift+H); tabs with section chips and button shelves instead of long menus; the 2D timeline with box select, Ctrl+A/C/V on keys, Clear all, row remove and restore, fold and zoom. The 3D view now shows the set, props, scenery, effects, reactions and storytime pieces in the Doodle look: click any of them (or Bunny) and drag the gizmo to move, turn or scale it (Q W E R), and the render puts it in the same place. Library cards have big previews; pointing at a motion or face plays it on Bunny. New props stand beside Bunny, clear of him.",
 "runtime": "44.9.0",
 "published": "2026-10-30T17:58:52.884Z",
